    "warranty": "NOT confirmed for residential air-to-air splits. Daikin UK installer warranty page: standard commercial warranty 'typically 1 or 3 years depending on product type'; Daikin UK Certified Installers 'up to 5 years on AC equipment'; D1/D1+ partners 'up to 7 years on AC equipment' (exact terms behind the Daikin Partner Portal). Daikin UK residential Stand By Me pages describe a free 2 -> 5 year extension when the installer registers the install, but that text is written for air-to-water heat pumps; the July 2025 residential end-user policy (third-party hosted copy) says installer registers on Stand By Me within 90 days of commissioning, customer activates within 24 months, annual maintenance required. UK retailer claims vary: some list Daikin splits with a '3 years manufacturer's parts warranty' (e.g. Rimy, FTXF35E/RXF35E), but Air Conditioning World lists FTXM25R/RXM25R9 with a 5-year manufacturer parts warranty (https://www.airconditioningworld.co.uk/daikin-ftxm25r-rxm25r9-2-5kw-, search extract recorded in docs/research/data/equipment-prices.json, not live-verified). Confirm the air-to-air terms and the Certified Installer route with Daikin UK before quoting customers.",
    "notes": "Daikin FTXF-F/RXF-F table: cooling nominal 5.0 kW (max 5.3), heating nominal 5.4 kW (max 6.13), EER 3.30, COP 3.71, SEER 6.50, SCOP 4.10, 269 kWh/a cooling. No Lot 10 label for this exact pair was found in search, so energy classes are derived from the EU 626/2011 thresholds (SEER 6.1-8.5 = A++; SCOP 4.0-4.6 = A+), not read from a label. Sound pressure cooling silent/low/med/high 31/34/39/45 dB(A); sound power 59. Daikin tables put the 50 in the same 286x770x225 mm body as the 20-42 classes (9 kg) - surprising, so check before planning a wall position. Pipe 1/4in liquid, 1/2in gas (FTXF50F installation manual). Retail seen in UK: City Plumbing (RXF50F), Basildon ACR (pair ~GBP 830 inc VAT - generation doubtful, see fact-check). Some retailers still quote the older FTXF50D/RXF50D (SEER 6.21) - different model. All figures were read from search-engine extracts of the cited Daikin pages/PDFs (direct page fetch was DNS-blocked in the research sandbox); spot-check against the PDF before quoting. fact-check (2026-10-18): Wi-Fi 'built in on UK stock' is contested by a UK retailer (Basildon ACR, 'wifi-optional'); not confirmed either way. fact-check (2026-10-18): the Basildon ACR URL cited for the ~GBP 830 pair price is '.../ftxf50d-rxf50d-5-0kw-...-wifi-optional/', i.e. the older FTXF50D/RXF50D that this record says is a different model, so the price may not apply to FTXF50F/RXF50F. City Plumbing's RXF50F ~GBP 820 has no stated VAT basis. Use neither as an F-generation trade price. COST (synthesizer): no public price observation for this exact model or its pair kit in docs/research/data/equipment-prices.json or the brand files, so costPence is null. City Plumbing RXF50F ~GBP 820 (VAT basis not stated) and Basildon ACR pair ~GBP 830 inc VAT (URL names older FTXF50D/RXF50D) exist, but the Daikin fact-check says use neither as an F-generation price; costPence stays null.",
